<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00395</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>abae7b48-72bc-4f59-ae0e-56747e1f72d4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="e9b02bb9-8c65-4892-97c8-2205bdb22357" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1f209805-d7b2-47b1-8d9f-e26f07909497" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((5,15)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((20,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,20)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(45,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((5,15)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following points is the solution to the system of equations that is graphed?<figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f8b2817150ab876b42893d7d192fa7208d9b2dfc"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The two points intersect at the point \((5,15)\) so that is the solution of the system.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7b734813-1789-4f31-8e93-148a0efa37d1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((5,2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((5,2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((2,5)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((8,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((5.2,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following points is the solution to the system of equations that is graphed?<figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/33de84819a3f6bb93578fdc791adb33bc752fc40"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The two points intersect at the point \((5, 2)\) so that is the solution of the system.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4ce91135-8284-4df5-b5c7-bd005f637908" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(y=\\frac12x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=4x-2\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=\\frac12x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=4x-2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=\\frac14x+2\\)&quot;,&quot;\\(y=\\frac{-1}{2}x+1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What two equations are represented by the graph? Select <emphasis>two</emphasis>.<figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8bbab63874107229f204df779b103cf9cc8e4dce"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The system of equations includes \(y=\frac12x-1\) and \(y=4x-2\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="357cb642-ec02-46bd-8cfd-1e9a42dc417a" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(y=x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=3x-2\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=x+1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=\\frac13x+2\\)&quot;,&quot;\\(y=3x-2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What two equations are represented by the graph? Select<emphasis> two</emphasis>.<figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/475020aab78e3fc53257a802ab6832ed21f34470"/></media></figure></para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The system of equations includes \(y=x-1\) and \(y=3x-2\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.--> <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>For questions 5 – 8, use the following scenario and matching table.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A streaming service has two different membership plans. Option A charges $10 per month plus $5 for each movie. Option B charges $20 a month then $2 a movie.</para>
</blockquote>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>Number of movies in a month, \(x\).</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>0</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>1</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>2</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>3</para>
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        <para>4</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
        <para>Option A</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>10</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>15</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>20</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>25</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>30</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
        <para>Option B</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>20</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>22</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>24</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>26</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>28</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="bad9b734-33b3-4b91-b02c-0003bf3aed80" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a77aa2bc-c28c-4a82-bce2-f92d629bcdf3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(Option\;\ A: 10\\ Option\;\ B: 20\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: 10\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: 20\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: 20\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: 10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: 5\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: 2\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: 5\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the \(y\)-intercept for Option A and Option B? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercepts are Option A = 10 and Option B = 20.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d22fc5ee-0e88-4a81-a45f-ed0a3765594e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(Option\;\ A: m =5\\ Option\;\ B: m =2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: \\frac{52}x=9\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: m =\\frac 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: m=2\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: m =5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: m =\\frac12\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: m =\\frac15\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(Option\\;\\ A: m =5\\\\ Option\\;\\ B: m =2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the slope of Option A and Option B? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The slopes are Option A = 5 and Option B = 2.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f1b30519-391e-4428-9902-f50ed11086aa" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(y=5x+10\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=10x+5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x-10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x+10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=10x-5\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the equation of Option A?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="79950d77-b1c9-45cf-aa22-18aa372b6184" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="\(y=2x+20\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=5x+20\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=2x+20\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=5x+10\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y=2x+10\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the equation of Option B?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The equation of the line for Option A is \(y=5x+10\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>For questions 9 - 12, use the following situation and graph.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>A family buys a total of 32 tickets at a carnival. Ride tickets cost $1.50 each and food tickets cost $3.25 each. The family pays a total of $90 for the tickets. The situation is graphed below.</para>
  <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eb44767d0c6710228091a100debe7800c1ed2a24"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>The \(x\)-axis represents the number of ride tickets and the \(y\)-axis represents the number of food tickets.</para>
</blockquote>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="93e88705-c740-4445-8a3d-d12cda94f625" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e7633643-d341-4b95-9151-a83dc6c45559" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="The orange, solid line" data-solution-options="[&quot;The orange, solid line&quot;, &quot;The blue, dashed line&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which line depicts the equation that represents the statement “A family buys a total of 32 tickets at a carnival”?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      Correct! The orange, solid line represents \(x + y = 32\).
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      Try again. Think about how the total number of tickets relates to the equation.
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d676f4bf-d5af-4c8f-865e-448984b5155a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="1.50x + 3.25y = 90" data-solution-options="[&quot;1.50x + 3.25y = 90&quot;, &quot;3.25x + 1.50y = 90&quot;, &quot;(1.50 + 3.25)x = 90y&quot;, &quot;(1.50 + 3.25)y = 90x&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>The remaining line represents the statements “Ride tickets cost $1.50 each and food tickets cost $3.25 each. The family pays a total of $90 for the tickets.” Which equation corresponds to these statements and the remaining line?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      Correct! The blue, dashed line represents the equation \(1.50x + 3.25y = 90\).
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      Not quite right. Consider the cost of each ticket type and the total amount spent.
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7984860e-cdd8-4802-aa9d-f49cb162dbc9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="8" data-solution-options="[&quot;32&quot;, &quot;60&quot;, &quot;7&quot;, &quot;24&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the approximate number of ride tickets the family purchased?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The two lines intersect at approximately \((8, 24)\) and the \(x\)-value represents the number of ride tickets which is 8.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#12-->
  <exercise data-content-id="63f44116-78d4-4a5c-93fb-b8834627837e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="24" data-solution-options="[&quot;32&quot;, &quot;60&quot;, &quot;7&quot;, &quot;24&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the approximate number of food tickets the family purchased?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The two lines intersect at (8,24) and the y-value represents the number of food tickets which is 24.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.2.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
